From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] leds: add Broadcom BCA CLED controller

Newer Broadcom BCA SoCs like BCM47622 have an LED controller that is
not register compatible with the one handled by leds-bcm63138: every
LED has its own configuration block holding the brightness and the
flash rate, which takes effect once the LED is activated. Add a driver
for its parallel LEDs.

The driver itself lives in target/linux/bcmbca/files.

Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/leds/blink/Kconfig  | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 drivers/leds/blink/Makefile |  1 +
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/leds/blink/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/Kconfig
@@ -12,6 +12,23 @@
 
 	  If compiled as module it will be called leds-bcm63138.
 
+config LEDS_BCMBCA_CLED
+	tristate "LED support for the Broadcom BCA CLED controller"
+	depends on LEDS_CLASS
+	depends on ARCH_BCMBCA || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on HAS_IOMEM
+	depends on OF
+	default ARCH_BCMBCA
+	help
+	  This option enables support for the "CLED" LED controller found in
+	  newer Broadcom BCA SoCs such as BCM47622. Its register layout differs
+	  from the controller supported by LEDS_BCM63138.
+
+	  Parallel LEDs with software brightness control and hardware
+	  blinking are supported.
+
+	  If compiled as module it will be called leds-bcmbca-cled.
+
 config LEDS_LGM
        tristate "LED support for LGM SoC series"
        depends on X86 || COMPILE_TEST
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/Makefile
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 obj-$(CONFIG_LEDS_BCM63138)	+= leds-bcm63138.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_LEDS_BCMBCA_CLED)	+= leds-bcmbca-cled.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_LEDS_LGM)	+= leds-lgm-sso.o
